(4394401, 630073, 72318, '<td valign="top">Severe purple fringing let this image down a lot, the quality / clarity isnt there either. I realise these are technical rather than artistic criticisms, but they can both be reduced past the level presented here, if not in postwork but in use of whatever camera you have. Nice out of the box concept but doesnt really say "clown" to me unless you read the title which is infact an idiom, so is only related to clowns in an abstract manner anyway.</td>', 'Severe purple fringing let this image down a lot, the quality / clarity isnt there either. I realise these are technical rather than artistic criticisms, but they can both be reduced past the level presented here, if not in postwork but in use of whatever camera you have. Nice out of the box concept but doesnt really say "clown" to me unless you read the title which is infact an idiom, so is only related to clowns in an abstract manner anyway.', '2008-01-15 18:11:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4394403, 630784, 72318, '<td valign="top">image is too dark, lighting is a bit weird, i dont get the title, slightly out of focus/motion blurred (cant tell which) and the composition is a bit unsettling.  "Confused viewer"<br/>Just putting down some thoughts to help you in what must be a low scoring entry.</td>', 'image is too dark, lighting is a bit weird, i dont get the title, slightly out of focus/motion blurred (cant tell which) and the composition is a bit unsettling.  "Confused viewer"Just putting down some thoughts to help you in what must be a low scoring entry.', '2008-01-15 18:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4394410, 630300, 72318, '<td valign="top">Using on-board flash is an unforgivable sin in my opinion when doing portraiture. Not only does it flatten all the features, but when used with the subject close to any background you get the horrible sharp shadow haloing the subject.<br/>When looking at this shot, it seems there was no effort put in: pair of joke glasses, kid, lie on floor, take picture with off-centre composition without thought for lighting.  There isnt any impact here.<br/> <br/>Just trying to help you with my thoughts on why i scored this low.</td>', 'Using on-board flash is an unforgivable sin in my opinion when doing portraiture. Not only does it flatten all the features, but when used with the subject close to any background you get the horrible sharp shadow haloing the subject.When looking at this shot, it seems there was no effort put in: pair of joke glasses, kid, lie on floor, take picture with off-centre composition without thought for lighting.  There isnt any impact here. Just trying to help you with my thoughts on why i scored this low.', '2008-01-15 18:18:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(4394416, 629707, 72318, '<td valign="top">so no real creative image concept to interest or speak to me, except the intended pun in the title. Try using desk lamps rather than the onboard flash to light this "product shot" style image, the lighting will really help give the shot some impact if you blow out the background and light the subject from the sides. Centre placement also doesnt do this image any favours, nor does the fact that the "Jewels" arent really given as much pride of place that the title suggests.<br/> <br/> <br/>Just trying to help you with my thoughts on why i scored this low.</td>', 'so no real creative image concept to interest or speak to me, except the intended pun in the title. Try using desk lamps rather than the onboard flash to light this "product shot" style image, the lighting will really help give the shot some impact if you blow out the background and light the subject from the sides. Centre placement also doesnt do this image any favours, nor does the fact that the "Jewels" arent really given as much pride of place that the title suggests.  Just trying to help you with my thoughts on why i scored this low.', '2008-01-15 18:23:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4394423, 630807, 88962, '<td valign="top">i thought that this was a very clever idea.</td>', 'i thought that this was a very clever idea.', '2008-01-15 18:32:27.000000', NULL, 1),
