(4402391, 629950, 87968, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Goes to show that it''s more the photographer than the equipment to produce great shots</td>', 'Congrats! Goes to show that it''s more the photographer than the equipment to produce great shots', '2008-01-18 10:49:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4402710, 630275, 66641, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone.  Yes, it is quite blurry.  I''m glad I submitted this though.  I''m just starting to learn about photography, and it''s great to hear all the comments and criticism, very eye opening.  In a sea of about 100 clown pictures that I tried to take, I actually couldn''t see that this was blurry.  After looking at the other pictures on DP, it was quite apparent right away what was wrong with the picture.  I guess my first goal should be to learn about focus.<br/> <br/>I have no idea about lighting as well.  I couldn''t even tell you one thing about the subject.  So I think that would be a good subject to read up on also.<br/> <br/>BeeCee - thank you for your suggestion, I would never have seen it.  But I completely agree with you, this would have been much better if the gumballs took up most of the space to the right of the clown.  As soon as I read that, the light went on for me.<br/> <br/>Tammer - Crazy, but I didn''t even notice the circles on the clowns outfit and how that could go together with the gumballs.  Again, as soon I read that the light went on.  Very important lesson for me, to pay attention to small details that can really enhance a picture.<br/> <br/>Thank you for all of the other comments.  I will start reading up on "bounce flashes", "diffusers", "fill light", and "levels work", whatever all that stuff may be!  :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-18 13:39:11.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone.  Yes, it is quite blurry.  I''m glad I submitted this though.  I''m just starting to learn about photography, and it''s great to hear all the comments and criticism, very eye opening.  In a sea of about 100 clown pictures that I tried to take, I actually couldn''t see that this was blurry.  After looking at the other pictures on DP, it was quite apparent right away what was wrong with the picture.  I guess my first goal should be to learn about focus. I have no idea about lighting as well.  I couldn''t even tell you one thing about the subject.  So I think that would be a good subject to read up on also. BeeCee - thank you for your suggestion, I would never have seen it.  But I completely agree with you, this would have been much better if the gumballs took up most of the space to the right of the clown.  As soon as I read that, the light went on for me. Tammer - Crazy, but I didn''t even notice the circles on the clowns outfit and how that could go together with the gumballs.  Again, as soon I read that the light went on.  Very important lesson for me, to pay attention to small details that can really enhance a picture. Thank you for all of the other comments.  I will start reading up on "bounce flashes", "diffusers", "fill light", and "levels work", whatever all that stuff may be!  :)', '2008-01-18 13:38:40.000000', '2008-01-18 13:39:11.000000', 0),
